From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: hub: recover connect events on powered but
 runtime-suspended ports

port_event() begins its action phase with

        /* skip port actions that require the port to be powered on */
        if (!pm_runtime_active(&port_dev->dev))
                return;

The premise of that check is that a runtime-suspended usb_port device
means the port was powered off, so nothing can be connected and any
event bits are noise.  That premise normally holds: with the default
PM_QOS_FLAG_NO_POWER_OFF request in place usb_port_runtime_suspend()
returns -EAGAIN, so a powered port can never reach RPM_SUSPENDED.

On CIX Sky1 (cdnsp-sky1/cdnsp-plat ACPI bring-up) some ports come out
of boot with that invariant already broken: the usb_port device is
RPM_SUSPENDED although port power was never dropped.  Measured on both
boards (O6N and MS-R1 r249), non-deterministically per port:

    usb11-port1  runtime_status=suspended  runtime_active_time=0
                 pm_qos_no_power_off=1     PORTSC.PP=1

runtime_active_time=0 over a 26h uptime shows the port was never
RPM_ACTIVE for even 1ms, while its sibling created by a later
controller rebind stays permanently active.  The suspend callback
kprobe never fires across full port lifecycles, so the state is not
reached through usb_port_runtime_suspend() -- the boot-time bring-up
leaves it that way (same window that prints the ten "runtime PM trying
to activate child device CIXH2031:0N but parent is not active"
warnings).

Once a port is in that state every connect on it is discarded forever:

  - hotplug of a VIA VL812 USB3 hub enumerates its SuperSpeed half on
    the paired SS port (active) while the USB2 companion port latches
    CCS but the CSC event is consumed with no action; the port parks at
    PORTSC 0x0c0006e1 = CCS=1 PED=0 PLS=Polling.
  - hub_activate() correctly reconciles the connection into
    change_bits on every root-hub resume ("status 0101 change 0000",
    then hub_event "chg 0002"), hub_event() runs port_event(), and the
    event dies on the pm_runtime_active() check.  Verified live with
    dynamic debug: the hub_port_connect_change() entry debug line is
    never reached.
  - the only recovery was a full controller unbind/rebind
    (ncz-usb2-rescan workaround, 15.6s of dead keyboard at boot).

Fix: only skip when port power is genuinely off.  hub->power_bits
tracks logical port power (usb_hub_set_port_power()).  If the bit is
set the port cannot be powered off, so the RPM_SUSPENDED status is
stale; resume the port device and handle the event instead of
dropping it.  For genuinely powered-off ports (power_bits clear)
behaviour is unchanged.  usb_port_runtime_resume() on an
already-powered childless port only re-issues
SetPortFeature(PORT_POWER) and sleeps the power-good delay.

Validated live on O6N: with the stuck VL812 attached, manually
resuming usb11-port1 and re-running the hub_activate()/hub_event()
cycle -- exactly what this patch automates -- enumerated the USB2 hub
half, keyboard and mouse within 300ms, portsc 0x00000e03 (PED, U0).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/core/hub.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
@@ -5829,9 +5829,33 @@
 				USB_PORT_FEAT_C_PORT_CONFIG_ERROR);
 	}
 
-	/* skip port actions that require the port to be powered on */
-	if (!pm_runtime_active(&port_dev->dev))
-		return;
+	/*
+	 * Skip port actions that require the port to be powered on, but only
+	 * when port power is genuinely off.  The runtime-PM state of the port
+	 * device is supposed to mirror logical port power: while the default
+	 * PM_QOS_FLAG_NO_POWER_OFF request is in place,
+	 * usb_port_runtime_suspend() refuses to run, so a powered port stays
+	 * RPM_ACTIVE.  If platform bring-up nevertheless leaves the port
+	 * device RPM_SUSPENDED while port power was never dropped (power_bits
+	 * still set), every connect-change on that port would be discarded
+	 * here forever: hub_activate() re-reports the connection into
+	 * change_bits on every resume, hub_event() runs, and the event dies
+	 * on this check with the port stuck at CCS=1/PED=0/PLS=Polling.
+	 *
+	 * A port whose power_bits entry is set cannot actually be powered
+	 * off, so treat suspended-but-powered as stale state and repair it
+	 * instead of dropping the event.  usb_port_runtime_resume() on an
+	 * already-powered childless port only re-issues
+	 * SetPortFeature(PORT_POWER) and waits out the power-good delay.
+	 */
+	if (!pm_runtime_active(&port_dev->dev)) {
+		if (!test_bit(port1, hub->power_bits))
+			return;
+		dev_info(&port_dev->dev,
+			 "port is powered but runtime-suspended; resuming it to handle the event\n");
+		if (pm_runtime_resume(&port_dev->dev) < 0)
+			return;
+	}
 
 	/* skip port actions if ignore_event and early_stop are true */
 	if (port_dev->ignore_event && port_dev->early_stop)
-- 
